<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tajarib al-umam</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Experiences of the Nations</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tajarib al-umam, 'Experiences of the Nations', is a universal history written in Arabic by the Persian scholar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miskawayh">Miskawayh</a>, who served as librarian to Buyid rulers and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">viziers</a>. Running from the Flood to 980, it is especially valuable as an eyewitness source for the Buyid period. Miskawayh, a philosopher, aimed to draw practical lessons from events rather than legends, which set the work apart from earlier chronicles.</p></div>
